I go into a very bustling clothing shop.
I need a raincoat for the heavy Mumbai rain.
I go to a shopkeeper.
I say to him, "Bhaiya, please show me a good raincoat."
The shopkeeper shows me a yellow raincoat.
He says, "Madam, look at this, this is very good."
I look at the yellow raincoat carefully.
This raincoat is very small and light.
I say, "Bhaiya, this is small for me."
"Do you have a raincoat bigger than this?"
The shopkeeper shows me a thick blue raincoat.
He says, "Madam, look at this blue raincoat."
"This is much stronger than that yellow raincoat."
I compare both raincoats.
The blue raincoat is really bigger than the yellow one.
It looks absolutely perfect for the Mumbai rain.
I smile and say, "I want this blue one."
I give the money for the raincoat.
